          "message": "fix: update FlatBuffer converter to use new unique_ptr-based VW initialize API (#4733)\n\n* fix: update FlatBuffer converter to use new unique_ptr-based VW initialize API\n\nUpdates the FlatBuffer text-to-flat converter to use the new unique_ptr-based\nVW::initialize() API instead of the deprecated raw pointer version.\n\nChanges:\n- Updated setup() to return std::unique_ptr<VW::workspace> instead of raw pointer\n- Changed alls vector to store unique_ptrs instead of raw pointers\n- Maintains existing functionality while using modern VW API\n\nThis resolves the deprecation warning:\n'VW::workspace* VW::initialize(...)' is deprecated: Replaced with new\nunique_ptr based overload.\n\nFixes warnings in: asan workflow (Linux)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: remove custom deleter from setup function signature\n\nThe VW::initialize() API now returns std::unique_ptr<workspace> and\nexpects std::unique_ptr<options_i> as input. The custom deleter is no\nlonger needed since the new API handles ownership properly.\n\nChanges:\n- Remove VW::options_deleter_type from setup() function signature\n- Use std::make_unique<options_cli> instead of manual construction\n- This eliminates the \"no viable overloaded '='\" error\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: use C++11-compatible unique_ptr construction\n\nReplace std::make_unique with direct unique_ptr construction using\nnew operator. std::make_unique is only available from C++14 onwards,\nbut VW defaults to C++11.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
