          "distinct": true,
          "id": "09f1e60ac441a972aab469dbe9276318162cde40",
          "message": "fix: address multiple CI warnings (#4738)\n\n* fix: use raw strings for regex patterns to avoid invalid escape sequences\n\nPython 3.12+ warns about invalid escape sequences in non-raw strings.\nThe \\- sequence in regex patterns should be in raw strings.\n\nFixes SyntaxWarning at lines 48 and 133.\n\n* fix: add save_load implementation for large action space template class\n\nProvides a stub implementation of save_load method to satisfy MSVC's\nexplicit template instantiation requirements. This fixes MSVC warning\nC4661 about missing suitable definition for template instantiation.\n\nThe method is currently a no-op as no state needs to be persisted.\n\n* fix: set CMake policies to suppress warnings\n\nSets the following CMake policies:\n- CMP0167: Use CONFIG mode for FindBoost with Boost 1.70+\n- CMP0169: Use timestamps from archives in FetchContent\n- CMP0087: Enable generator expression support in install(CODE/SCRIPT)\n\nThis eliminates policy-related warnings from vcpkg and build system.\n\n* fix: use difference_type for iterator subtraction operator\n\nChange action_scores_score_iterator::operator- to return difference_type\n(long) instead of size_t. This conforms to C++ iterator requirements where\nthe difference operator must return a signed integer type.\n\nFixes MSVC C4267 warning about conversion from 'size_t' to 'long' that\nwas triggered in xutility when STL algorithms used this custom iterator.",
          "timestamp": "2026-01-14T15:54:40-05:00",
