          "distinct": true,
          "id": "14f86dfde69198351c3fe1d4bb7e1131ae798095",
          "message": "fix: address CI warnings (revert codecvt, Boost.Bind, vcpkg cache) (#4742)\n\n* Revert \"fix: replace deprecated codecvt with manual UTF-16 to UTF-8 conversion (#4732)\"\n\nThis reverts commit 73dbc06bcc0da502e7bf39e23f7f104e5aa7dbc3.\n\n* fix: suppress Boost.Bind global placeholders deprecation warning\n\nAdd BOOST_BIND_GLOBAL_PLACEHOLDERS definition to Python bindings to\nsuppress the deprecation warning about global namespace placeholders.\n\nThis is a temporary fix. The proper solution is to migrate to using\n`boost::placeholders` namespace, but that requires updating Boost.Python\nheader includes which are external to our codebase.\n\nFixes warning: \"The practice of declaring the Bind placeholders (_1, _2, ...)\nin the global namespace is deprecated.\"\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: update vcpkg binary cache configuration to avoid deprecation warning\n\nReplace deprecated VCPKG_DEFAULT_BINARY_CACHE with VCPKG_BINARY_SOURCES\nusing the new 'clear;files,<path>,readwrite' format as recommended.\n\nThis resolves the deprecation warning:\n\"The VCPKG_DEFAULT_BINARY_CACHE environment variable is now deprecated\"\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
