          "distinct": true,
          "id": "5f46fab1bd2342bca268ccf6c2ff186238fd2d28",
          "message": "fix: suppress MSVC C4661, C4117, and C5308 warnings for automl and managed C++ (#4752)\n\n* fix: suppress MSVC C4661, C4117, and C5308 warnings for automl and managed C++\n\nSuppress MSVC warnings that are intentional:\n\n1. C4661: Template methods split across automl_impl.cc and automl_iomodel.cc\n   - Added /wd4661 to vw_core target\n   - Removed ineffective pragma from automl_iomodel.cc\n\n2. C4117/C5308: Modifying reserved macro '_M_CEE' for managed C++ compatibility\n   - Added /wd4117 and /wd5308 to vw_core and vw_allreduce targets\n   - object_pool.h and allreduce.h intentionally modify _M_CEE to work around\n     managed C++ limitations when including mutex/condition_variable headers\n   - C4117 in older MSVC versions, C5308 in VS2022+\n\n* fix: suppress C5308 warnings in header pragmas for VS2022\n\nThe pragmas in object_pool.h and allreduce.h were only suppressing C4117\n(older MSVC), but VS2022 uses C5308 for the same warning about modifying\nthe _M_CEE reserved macro. This was causing warnings in the nuget build.\n\nAdded C5308 to the pragma warning disable directives in both headers.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-01-15T23:02:41-05:00",
