          "distinct": true,
          "id": "f18c4e61964a9fc9126c5727f97e0ca663e219fb",
          "message": "fix: eliminate C4244 type conversion warnings in test code and topk (#4757)\n\nMSVC generates C4244 warnings when implicit type conversions lose precision\n(e.g., double→float, size_t→int). Fixed 136 warnings across 4 files:\n\n1. **eigen_memory_tree_test.cc** (41 fixes)\n   - Changed `std::make_pair(int, int/double)` to use proper types\n   - Now uses `uint64_t{n}` for indices and `f` suffix for floats\n   - Matches `emt_feats = std::vector<std::pair<uint64_t, float>>`\n\n2. **igl_simulator.h** (6 fixes)\n   - Changed integer/double literals to float literals with `f` suffix\n   - Fixed `std::map<std::string, float>` initializers\n\n3. **simulator.cc** (1 fix)\n   - Added explicit cast from `size_t` to `int` in return statement\n   - Function returns `std::pair<int, float>` but used `size_t` index\n\n4. **topk.cc** (1 fix)\n   - Changed `std::accumulate` initial value from `0` to `size_t{0}`\n   - Prevents implicit conversion during accumulation\n\nEliminates all C4244 warnings:\n- Windows 2022: 126 warnings (63 Debug + 63 Release)\n- Windows 2019: 10 warnings (5 Debug + 5 Release)",
          "timestamp": "2026-01-16T08:22:44-05:00",
          "tree_id": "43acb0296e4558621763d6f371a1f40986b93515",
          "url": "https://github.com/VowpalWabbit/vowpal_wabbit/commit/f18c4e61964a9fc9126c5727f97e0ca663e219fb"
