          "distinct": true,
          "id": "6dc556308e9b02d1ac56bd8b70427511278bbf7c",
          "message": "fix: combined Python improvements and bug fixes (#4773)\n\n* fix: add integer overflow checks in sync_queries() to prevent buffer overflow\n\nAdd overflow checks when calculating total_sum and prev_sum in\nsync_queries() function (kernel_svm.cc). Without these checks, an\nattacker could manipulate input data to cause integer overflow,\nresulting in undersized buffer allocation and subsequent buffer overflow.\n\nFixes #4717\n\n* fix: update statistics for final partial batch in LDA minibatch mode\n\nWhen using LDA with --minibatch > 1, the final partial batch was\nprocessed for learning in end_pass() but not counted in reported\nstatistics. This is because update_stats_lda() only updates stats\nwhen batch_buffer.size() == minibatch, excluding partial batches.\n\nAdd stats update in end_pass() after learn_batch() to ensure the\nfinal partial batch examples are counted.\n\nAlso update test reference files to reflect the corrected example counts:\n- wiki1K.stderr: 256 -> 384 examples (128 final batch now counted)\n- no_label_fb.stderr: 256 -> 384 examples\n- lda-2pass-hang.stderr: 500 -> 501 examples per pass\n- wiki1K_no_minibatch.stderr: 256 -> 257 examples\n\nFixes #4719\n\n* fix: remove importlib_metadata fallback for Python < 3.8\n\nSince the project now requires Python 3.10+ (as defined in pyproject.toml),\nthe fallback to the third-party importlib_metadata package for Python < 3.8\nis no longer needed. This simplifies the code and removes an unnecessary\nruntime dependency check.\n\nFixes #4718\n\n* docs: document Python version support (3.10-3.13)\n\nAdd explicit Python version documentation:\n- Update setup.py classifiers to list Python 3.10, 3.11, 3.12, 3.13\n- Add python_requires=\">=3.10\" to setup.py\n- Add Requirements section to Python README listing supported versions\n- Document pre-built wheel availability for Linux, macOS, and Windows\n\nThis addresses user confusion about which Python versions are supported\nfor pip installation.\n\nFixes #4714\n\n* feat: enable CSV parsing in vcpkg builds and run help tests\n\nEnable VW_FEAT_CSV in vcpkg-debug and vcpkg-release presets so that\nthe --help output includes CSV parser options, matching the test\nreference files. This allows tests 275 and 276 to pass.",
