          "distinct": true,
          "id": "342e456aeab4ece27aed3afde286f6a821fe7789",
          "message": "feat: combined Python improvements and bug fixes (#4779)\n\n* feat: combined Python improvements and bug fixes\n\nThis PR combines the following improvements:\n\n1. **Weak reference for memory leak fix** (from #4771)\n   - py_log_wrapper uses weakref.ref to avoid reference cycles\n   - _log_fwd can be safely cleared in finish() to free memory\n   - Callbacks gracefully skip if Python object is garbage collected\n\n2. **Dual-channel logging** (from #4778)\n   - Separate driver output (progress, stats) from logger output (warnings, errors)\n   - New methods: get_driver_output(), get_log_output()\n   - Backward compatible: get_log() returns combined output\n\n3. **fmt 11 compatibility** (from #4775)\n   - Add missing fmt/ranges.h include for fmt 11\n\n4. **--eval option persistence** (from #4776)\n   - Add .keep() to --eval option so it persists in model files\n\n5. **sklearn unsigned int support** (from #4777)\n   - Support unsigned integers in sklearn tovw function\n   - Converts uint to int64 to avoid overflow issues\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: save separate driver/logger logs for get_driver_output/get_log_output after finish()\n\nThe get_driver_output() and get_log_output() methods would fail after\nfinish() was called because _log_fwd is cleared. This fix:\n\n- Adds _saved_driver_log and _saved_logger_log fields\n- Saves separate logs in finish() before clearing _log_fwd\n- Updates get_driver_output() and get_log_output() to check saved logs\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-01-19T21:33:39-05:00",
