          "distinct": true,
          "id": "da9758d6c5fcf4c33feea75ae7f8157464dea9e5",
          "message": "fix: expose FTRL/Coin/PiSTOL config via get_config() (#4780)\n\n* fix: expose FTRL/Coin/PiSTOL config via get_config()\n\nAdd persist_metrics callback to FTRL learner builder to expose\nconfiguration through the metrics system, making it available via\nvw.get_config() in Python.\n\nExposed metrics:\n- ftrl_algorithm: Algorithm name (Proximal-FTRL, PiSTOL, Coin Betting)\n- ftrl_alpha: Learning rate parameter\n- ftrl_beta: Learning rate parameter\n- ftrl_size: State size (3, 4, or 6 depending on algorithm)\n- ftrl_total_weight: Total weight of examples seen\n- ftrl_normalized_sum_norm_x: Accumulated normalized norm\n\nFixes #4620\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: add tests for FTRL/PiSTOL/Coin metrics exposure\n\nTests verify that the persist_metrics function correctly exposes:\n- ftrl_algorithm (algorithm name)\n- ftrl_alpha, ftrl_beta (learning rate parameters)\n- ftrl_size (weight array size per algorithm)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: add C++ unit tests for FTRL metrics\n\nAdd ftrl_test.cc with tests for FTRL, PiSTOL, and Coin betting\nalgorithms to verify persist_metrics exposes the correct values.\nThis provides C++ code coverage for the persist_metrics function.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-01-20T17:09:19-05:00",
