          "distinct": true,
          "id": "f24774b9a3fa20bc23b8d133d2182d22b120c15e",
          "message": "test: add coverage tests for C wrapper and LDA readable_model (#4816)\n\n* test: add coverage tests for C wrapper and LDA readable_model\n\nAdd tests for:\n- VW_SeedWithModel C API function (creates seeded model from existing)\n- VW_SeedWithModel with test mode (-t flag)\n- LDA readable_model text output\n- UTF-16 to UTF-8 conversion in C wrapper\n\nThese tests cover previously uncovered code paths in:\n- c_wrapper/src/vwdll.cc (VW_SeedWithModel)\n- core/src/reductions/lda_core.cc (save_load with text=true)\n\n* test: add e2e test for memory_tree with OAS (multilabel)\n\nAdd end-to-end test for memory_tree reduction using OAS (One-Against-Some)\nmode with multilabel input format. This covers the OAS code paths in\nmemory_tree.cc that were previously uncovered.\n\n* test: add e2e tests for LDA readable_model and BFGS regularizer output\n\nAdd end-to-end tests for:\n- LDA with --readable_model output (test 474)\n- BFGS with --output_feature_regularizer_text (test 475)\n\nThese tests cover the text output code paths in:\n- lda_core.cc save_load with text=true\n- bfgs.cc regularizer output functionality\n\n* fix: add random_seed to LDA test for deterministic output\n\n* fix: use smaller LDA dataset to reduce cross-platform float variance\n\nUse 5-example dataset with 2 topics and larger minibatch to minimize\nfloating-point differences between platforms while still exercising\nthe readable_model code path.\n\n* fix: prevent null pointer in memory_tree over_lap function\n\nAdd early return when either array is empty to avoid passing null\npointer to qsort, which is undefined behavior. This fixes UBSAN\nerrors when running memory_tree with OAS mode.\n\n* fix: free regularizers array in bfgs destructor to prevent memory leak\n\nThe regularizers array was allocated in preconditioner_to_regularizer()\nbut never freed in the destructor, causing a memory leak detected by\nLeakSanitizer.\n\n* refactor: reduce BFGS test hash bits to shrink reference file\n\nUse -b 10 instead of default -b 18 to reduce bfgs_regularizer.txt\nfrom 266k lines to 2k lines.",
          "timestamp": "2026-01-24T18:18:59-05:00",
          "tree_id": "2354cd9e877ceb7c1bd0dc8b1406af3e9ed14cf2",
