          "distinct": true,
          "id": "c6853d9843e1ab224bdea44523ab7f8b39ef006e",
          "message": "test: add e2e tests for coverage expansion (#4823)\n\n* test: add e2e tests for coverage expansion\n\nAdd 13 new end-to-end tests covering various VW features:\n\n- Test 504: cb_explore_adf with cover exploration and audit\n- Test 505: search sequence with holdout_period and audit\n- Test 506: search entity_relation (LDF-based) with audit\n- Test 507: LDA with audit exercising get_top_weights\n- Test 508: BFGS with L1 regularizer\n- Test 509: kernel SVM with pool_greedy active learning\n- Test 510: GD with sparse_weights option\n- Test 511: using --keep option to filter namespaces\n- Test 512: csoaa_ldf with audit exercising output_cs_example\n- Test 513: main.cc --onethread option\n- Test 514: compressed .gz input file support\n- Test 515: readable_model output verification\n- Test 516: main.cc --args option for multi-model training\n\nThese tests target previously untested code paths in:\n- cb_explore_adf.cc (cover exploration)\n- search/ (holdout, audit, entity_relation)\n- lda_core.cc (get_top_weights via audit)\n- bfgs.cc (L1 regularization)\n- kernel_svm.cc (pool_greedy active learning)\n- gd.cc (sparse weights)\n- parse_args.cc (--keep option)\n- cost_sensitive.cc (output_cs_example via csoaa_ldf audit)\n- main.cc (--onethread, --args options)\n\n* fix: search_graph division by zero due to initialization order\n\nThe setup() function in search_graph.cc calculated D.multiplier using\nD.total_feature_width and D.ss before those values were initialized,\ncausing a division by zero (SIGFPE) when add_edge_features_single_fn\nor add_edge_features_group_fn attempted to divide by D.multiplier.\n\nFix: Move the multiplier calculation after the initialization of the\nvalues it depends on.\n\nAlso adds test 517 to verify search_graph functionality.\n\n* fix: remove audit from search tests for cross-platform stability\n\nTests 505 and 506 were using --audit which produces output that varies\nacross platforms due to feature hash ordering differences. Remove audit\nsince it's not essential to what these tests are validating (holdout_period\nand entity_relation functionality).\n\n* test: reduce dataset sizes to ≤25 lines and model sizes to 7 bits\n\n- Create smaller datasets: 0001_25.dat, 0002_25.dat, wsj_25.dat,\n  er_24.vw, ner_25.dat(.gz) with ≤25 lines each\n- Update tests 505-516 to use smaller datasets and -b 7 bit models\n  (except kernel SVM which requires -b 18)\n- Test 509 (kernel SVM) uses rcv1_25.dat but keeps -b 18 due to\n  assertion failures with smaller bit sizes\n- Reduces test execution time and reference file sizes",
          "timestamp": "2026-01-26T22:54:56-05:00",
          "tree_id": "d839e81ace955a7dab51e2d0f5167f403215a1a3",
