          "id": "4a8a19aa1f264323afd2668dd1e15ade3cc5cb00",
          "message": "test: add coverage tests for loss functions, initialization, C wrapper, and 53 E2E tests (#4839)\n\n* test: add coverage tests for loss functions, initialization, C wrapper, and 53 E2E tests (#4839)\n\nAdd comprehensive tests to increase code coverage:\n\nUnit tests:\n- loss_functions_test.cc: classic squared, hinge, quantile, and poisson loss\n- initialize_test.cc: string overload, escaped init, finish workspace\n- vwdll_test.cc: tag accessors, audit data, save model, topic/multilabel/\n  cost-sensitive/action-score predictions, feature accessors, finish passes\n\nE2E tests (ids 537-589):\n- Loss functions: quantile, expectile, classic loss with various parameters\n- Reductions: active learning, cs_active, log_multi, marginal save/load\n- Features: LDA audit, BFGS holdout, stagewise poly, CSV parser\n- Search: multiple search options coverage\n- Parser: JSON/DSJSON formats, cost-sensitive labels\n- Options: feature_limit, interactions, bootstrap, multilabel_oaa,\n  confidence, gzip input, test mode, quadratic/cubic, verbose output,\n  invert_hash, initial_weight, random/normal/truncated_normal weights\n\n* fix: resolve -Werror build failures in new tests\n\n- Replace deprecated VW::initialize(string), VW::initialize_escaped(),\n  and VW::finish() calls with non-deprecated equivalents\n- Remove unused pred_per_update variable in HingeLossTest\n\n* fix: add missing parse_primitives.h include for split_command_line\n\n* fix: disambiguate split_command_line call with explicit std::string\n\n* build: enable CSV parser in Python wheel builds\n\nThe CSV parser has no external dependencies and is self-contained,\nso it can be safely enabled across all platforms.\n\n* build: enable CSV parser in model check workflow wheel builds\n\n* test: remove --quiet from 35 new E2E tests and regenerate stderr refs\n\nRemove --quiet flag from new E2E tests (ids 549, 555-589) so their\nstderr output is validated against reference files, increasing test\ncoverage of VW's progress reporting paths.\n\n* fix: preserve loss function parameters when loading models in compat check\n\nAdd --quantile_tau and --expectile_q to keep_arg_commands so these\nrequired loss function sub-parameters are passed through when loading\nmodels in the forward/backward compatibility checks.\n\n* fix: skip marginal models in model compat weight comparison\n\nAdd --marginal to skip_weights_flags to prevent json_weights() from\nhanging on marginal models during forward/backward model compatibility\nchecks. The marginal reduction's internal state causes json_weights()\nto stall when loaded by a different VW version.\n\n* fix: add per-test timeout to model compat checks to prevent CI stalls\n\nUses SIGALRM with a 120s timeout around both generate_model_and_weights\nand load_model operations. If a single test exceeds the timeout, it is\nskipped with a warning rather than stalling the entire CI workflow.\n\n* fix: skip poisson loss models in model compat weight comparison\n\njson_weights() produces invalid JSON for poisson loss models in older\nVW versions, causing JSONDecodeError during cross-version model loading.\n\n* fix: prevent float overflow in poisson loss and remove timeout workaround\n\nThe poisson loss function could produce infinite weights when exp() or\nexpm1() overflowed float range. This caused json_weights() to produce\ntruncated/invalid JSON, breaking model compatibility checks.\n\nRoot cause: In get_update(), std::expm1(label * update_scale *\npred_per_update) overflows when adaptive learning produces large\npred_per_update values (from small past gradients). The overflow\ncascades to make the entire weight update -inf.\n\nFix in loss_functions.cc:\n- Add clamp_prediction() to limit exp() argument to ±44.0f\n  (exp(44)^2 < FLT_MAX, preventing overflow in get_square_grad)\n- In get_update(), detect when expm1 argument exceeds MAX_EXP_ARG\n  and use the analytical limit: -(pred - log(label)) / pred_per_update\n- Handle label==0 branch overflow with isfinite check\n\nThis fixes poisson training convergence (avg loss 0.010535 vs 13.703300)\nand produces valid finite weights, so the model compat check timeout\nworkaround and poisson skip are no longer needed.\n\nChanges to run_tests_model_gen_and_load.py:\n- Remove SIGALRM-based timeout mechanism (signal, _ModelLoadTimeout)\n- Remove \"--loss_function poisson\" from skip_weights_flags\n- Keep \"--marginal\" skip (cross-version issue unrelated to this fix)\n\n* fix: add explicit error for json_weights on marginal and ksvm models\n\njson_weights (dump_weights_to_json_experimental) only exports the base\nlearner weight array. For reductions like marginal (which stores state\nin a separate std::map) and KSVM (which uses support vectors), the\nexported weights are incomplete and do not represent the full model.\n\nWalk the reduction stack to detect marginal and log a clear error\nmessage via logger.err_error, returning an empty weights array. Also\nupgrade the existing KSVM and uninitialized-weights checks from\nlogger.warn to logger.err_error for consistency.\n\n* fix: restore timeout and poisson skip for cross-version model compat\n\nThe timeout and poisson skip cannot be removed yet because the cross-\nversion model compatibility check loads models using the old master VW\ncode, which has json_weights() bugs that cause hangs (e.g. tests 524,\n542) and invalid JSON for poisson models.\n\nThe timeout is only needed in load_model (cross-version path). The\ngenerate step always uses the current PR code which has the poisson\noverflow fix, but we still skip generating poisson weights since the\nload side (old master) cannot compare them.\n\nThese skips can be removed once the poisson loss fix from the previous\ncommit is merged into master.\n\n* fix: use exact limit for poisson get_update label=0 overflow case\n\nThe label=0 overflow branch was using -p/w as the substitute, which\ndrops the log(η·w)/w term from the exact limit -(p + log(η·w))/w.\nUse the full expression to be mathematically precise.",
