          "id": "ffabba324b886ee1a354cf62088864d7fe6cbb50",
          "message": "test: add 100 E2E tests, fix SVRG quiet-mode bug, fix graph feedback test macro (#4842)\n\n* test: add 64 E2E tests and fix graph feedback test macro for coverage increase\n\nAdd 64 new end-to-end tests (IDs 590-653) covering diverse reductions and\nfeatures: slates DSJSON, cbify warm_start, WAP LDF, csoaa_rank, interactions,\nnn/dropout, ftrl/pistol/coin, OjaNewton, gd_mf, boosting, memory_tree,\neigen_memory_tree, freegrad, cb_explore_adf cover/bag/regcb/rnd,\nJSON/DSJSON/CCB parsing, CSV, autolink, multilabel save/load, active_cover,\naudit_regressor, baseline, dep_parser, sequencespan BILOU, argmax, graph task,\ncb_explore, LDA math modes, search no_caching/mix_per_roll/xv/perturb_oracle,\nsvrg, generate_interactions, oaa named_labels, csoaa audit, affix features,\nand invert_hash.\n\nFix preprocessor guard in cb_graph_feedback_test.cc and\ncb_graph_feedback_label_parse_test.cc: VW_FEAT_CB_GRAPH_FEEDBACK ->\nVW_FEAT_CB_GRAPH_FEEDBACK_ENABLED to match cmake-generated macro, enabling\n18 previously-dead unit tests to compile and run.\n\n* fix: SVRG stable point commit skipped when --quiet flag is used\n\nThe SVRG learn() function gated weight initialization (copying inner\nweights to stable, zeroing stable gradients) behind `!quiet`, meaning\nthe stable point commit never happened in quiet mode. This caused SVRG\nto degenerate to vanilla SGD when --quiet was passed.\n\nSeparate the pass-transition logic from the quiet-gated log messages\nso weight initialization always happens regardless of quiet mode.\n\n* test: remove --quiet from E2E tests and update reference files\n\nRemove --quiet flag from all 64 new E2E tests (590-653) so stderr\nprogress output is validated. The test framework's fuzzy comparison\n(-f flag, epsilon=1e-4) handles platform-dependent float differences.\n\nUpdate reference files to include stderr progress output, and\nregenerate svrg test refs (643, 644) to reflect the fixed algorithm\nbehavior.\n\n* test: add 36 E2E tests for boosting, eigen memory tree, search, and more\n\nAdd E2E tests (IDs 654-689) targeting coverage gaps:\n- Boosting: logistic, adaptive, BBM algorithms with save/load (654-659)\n- Eigen memory tree: scorer types (random, distance, self_consistent_rank),\n  router types, initial types, tree bounding, leaf splits (660-666)\n- Search entity relation: custom skip cost, no constraints, custom costs (667-669)\n- Search options: rollout_num_steps, subsample_time, beta/alpha,\n  policy interpolation, condition_feature_value, save_every_k (670-675)\n- Stagewise poly: exponent/batch size variations (676-678)\n- Gradient descent: feature_limit, l1/l2, sparse_l2 (679-681)\n- LDA: custom alpha/rho, multi-topic (682-683)\n- Parser: save_per_pass (684)\n- Output: readable_model with invert_hash (685)\n- Kernel SVM: RBF/poly kernels, pool_greedy/reprocess (686-688)\n- CB DRO: distributionally robust optimization (689)\n\n* fix: resolve CI failures in E2E and unit tests for cross-platform compatibility\n\n- initialize_test.cc: wrap deprecated API calls in VW_WARNING_STATE_PUSH/\n  VW_WARNING_DISABLE_DEPRECATED_USAGE to fix -Werror=deprecated-declarations,\n  use raw pointer type with VW::finish() cleanup\n- loss_functions_test.cc: remove unused pred_per_update variable to fix\n  -Werror=unused-variable\n- active_cover.cc: use std::pow(q2, 1.5f) instead of pow(q2, 1.5) to avoid\n  float-to-double promotion causing platform-dependent results (test 615)\n- test 601: use smaller dataset (0002_25.dat) to reduce accumulated FP\n  divergence across platforms\n- tests 643-644: add --onethread to SVRG tests to eliminate race condition\n  between parser and learner threads reading passes_complete, which caused\n  non-deterministic stage transition messages across platforms\n\n* fix: wrap Finish.BasicFinish in deprecated warning suppression, use smaller dataset for test 615\n\n- initialize_test.cc: Finish.BasicFinish test also uses deprecated\n  VW::finish() API, wrap in VW_WARNING_STATE_PUSH/POP to fix clang++\n  -Werror=deprecated-declarations\n- test 615 (active_cover): switch from 0002.dat (1000 examples) to\n  0002_25.dat (25 examples) to reduce accumulated FP divergence that\n  causes different results on macOS/Windows vs Linux\n\n* perf: use small datasets (~25 examples) for E2E tests 590-689\n\nReplace large datasets with small equivalents to speed up test execution:\n- 0002.dat (1000) -> 0002_25.dat (25)\n- 0001.dat (200) -> 0001_25.dat (25)\n- rcv1_small.dat/rcv1_smaller.dat (250-1000) -> rcv1_25.dat (25)\n- wiki256.dat (256) -> wiki25.dat (25)\n- cb_test_medium.ldf (55) -> cb_test_small.ldf (22)\n- er_small.vw (36) -> er_small_25.vw (25)\n\nUpdates 40 tests and regenerates all reference stderr files.\n\n* fix: use simple well-separated dataset for kernel SVM tests\n\nThe ksvm tests (485-528, 686-688) used rcv1_25.dat which is\nhigh-dimensional sparse data causing cross-platform divergence.\nThe SVM's iterative optimization amplifies tiny floating-point\ndifferences between x86_64+AVX2 (Linux), x86_64+SSE2 (Windows),\nand ARM64+NEON (macOS), leading to completely different predictions.\n\nReplace with ksvm_simple.dat: 20 interleaved examples with 2\nwell-separated features. The low dimensionality (2 multiply-adds\nper dot product) minimizes FP accumulation differences, and the\nclear class separation ensures predictions stay far from the\ndecision boundary regardless of platform.",
