          "distinct": true,
          "id": "1fecfb2e708520627654b3975a68eff73efea84d",
          "message": "test: add 36 E2E tests for parsers, search, and coverage gaps (batch 5) (#4843)\n\n* test: add 36 E2E tests for parsers, search, and coverage gaps (batch 5)\n\nAdd E2E tests (IDs 690-725) targeting parser and remaining coverage gaps:\n- CSV parser: tab separator, no_file_header with custom header, namespace\n  value scaling, quoted fields (RFC-4180), audit mode (690-694)\n- JSON parser: CB with labelIndex/chain_hash, DSJSON CB default namespace,\n  CCB with outcomes/original_label_cost, CCB without event ID, CB with\n  pdrop/pdrop=1, features with zero values, CCB simple/pdrop, CCB automl,\n  CCB reuse dedup (695-705)\n- Slates: interactions with invert_hash (706)\n- Text parser: affix features, affix with audit (707-708)\n- Cost-sensitive: LDF shared header, LDF audit with noconstant (709-710)\n- Parser: cache create/reuse, JSON audit, DSJSON audit (711-712, 722-723)\n- Training options: holdout_period, early_terminate, min/max prediction,\n  logistic loss function (713-714, 724-725)\n- Search: allowed_transitions file, rollin/rollout oracle, rollin learn/\n  rollout none, max_bias_ngram_length (715-718)\n- BFGS: with passes and holdout (719)\n- Interactions: permutations mode (720)\n- Output: verbose P=1 (721)\n\nNew test data files: csv_tab.csv, csv_quoted.csv, csv_no_header.csv,\nsearch_allowed_transitions.txt\n\n* test: add unit tests for vw.cc C API, example utilities, and label parsers\n\nAdd 77 new unit tests targeting uncovered code paths:\n\n- vw_c_api_test.cc: Tests for C-style API getters (get_label,\n  get_prediction, get_importance, get_initial, get_cost_sensitive_prediction,\n  get_action_score, get_multilabel_predictions, get_tag, get_feature_number,\n  get_confidence, get_topic_prediction), mutators (add_label,\n  add_constant_feature), data operations (export_example,\n  release_feature_space, get_features, return_features, import_example),\n  example utilities (new_unused_example, move_feature_namespace,\n  copy_example_data, copy_example_metadata, copy_example_data_with_label,\n  empty_example), cmd_string_replace_value, seed_vw_model,\n  parse_example_label, and alloc/dealloc_examples.\n\n- example_utils_test.cc: Tests for swap_prediction (all prediction types),\n  to_string for scalars, flatten_features, append/truncate example\n  namespaces, return_multiple_example, and get_total_sum_feat_sq.\n\n- Extended cost_sensitive_label_test.cc: Tests for \"label\" keyword parse,\n  \"shared\" keyword parse, named labels (ldict) parsing, cache round-trip.\n\n- Extended multiclass_label_parser_test.cc: Tests for named labels parsing,\n  constructor/reset, weight edge cases, model serialization, cache\n  round-trip, and integration with --probabilities mode.\n\n* test: add targeted unit tests to close remaining coverage gaps\n\nAdd 9 tests in coverage_gap_test.cc targeting uncovered code in:\n- action_score.cc: operator<< for action_score\n- debug_print.cc: prob_dist_pred_to_string\n- ccb_label.cc: is_labeled, copy ctor/assignment with outcome, reset_to_default\n- distributionally_robust.cc: Duals and chi_squared model serialization\n- ccb_label.cc: cache label round-trip via label_parser\n\nCombined with prior unit and E2E tests, this brings core/src line\ncoverage from 89.9% to 90.1% (23351/25930 lines).\n\n* fix: use shlex to parse commands in model gen/load script\n\nThe model gen/load script passed command strings directly to\nvowpalwabbit.Workspace which uses naive str.split(), breaking\nshell-quoted arguments like --csv_separator '\\t'. Use shlex.split\n(matching the E2E test runner) so quotes are handled correctly.\n\n* fix: fix CSV separator test for Windows and search transitions segfault\n\n- Test 690: change from tab separator (requires shell quoting that\n  breaks on Windows) to semicolon separator, which works cross-platform.\n  Tab separator is already covered by the C++ unit test.\n- Test 715: fix search_allowed_transitions.txt to use colon-delimited\n  format (1:2) matching what VW's fscanf expects, instead of\n  space-delimited (1 2) which left 'to' uninitialized causing segfault.\n\n* fix: use delete[] for array allocated with new[] in release_feature_space\n\nThe features array in release_feature_space was allocated with\nnew primitive_feature_space[len] but freed with delete instead of\ndelete[]. This causes an alloc-dealloc mismatch caught by ASAN.\n\n* perf: use small datasets (~25 examples) for E2E tests 707-725",
