          "message": "test: unskip macOS ARM precision tests by reducing dataset sizes (#4850)\n\n* test: reduce dataset sizes to fix macOS ARM floating-point precision skips\n\nTests 109, 280-284 were skipped on macOS-14 (and cbzo tests on all\nASAN/UBSAN builds) due to floating-point precision divergence between\nx86_64 and ARM64 architectures.\n\nInstead of skipping, reduce the datasets to 25 examples each:\n- cbzo_linear_small.dat: 25 lines (from 500-line cbzo_linear.dat)\n- wsj_tiny.dparser.vw.gz: 25 tokens across 2 sentences (from 54 tokens)\n\nSmaller datasets produce less accumulated floating-point divergence,\nallowing tests to pass within epsilon=0.001 across all platforms.\n\nRemove all --skip_test directives for tests 109, 280, 282, 283, 284\nfrom build_macos.yml, asan.yml, and vendor_build.yml.\n\n* fix: handle range-separator dash in fuzzy float comparison\n\nThe cbzo prediction format uses '-' as a range separator between\nnumbers (e.g. \"-0.199--0.199:16777216,0.001-0.001:4294967296\").\nThe test tokenizer splits on [ \\t:,@=\\[\\]] but not '-', creating\ncompound tokens like \"-0.199--0.199\" that can't be parsed as floats\nand fall back to exact string comparison.\n\nAdd a lookbehind/lookahead pattern (?<=\\d)-(?=-?\\d) to split on '-'\nonly when it separates two numbers, preserving leading negative signs.\nThis allows fuzzy epsilon comparison to work correctly for cbzo and\nany other range-formatted prediction output.",
          "timestamp": "2026-02-01T12:30:29-05:00",
          "tree_id": "bd62a026c1db68a79968bc25cd83ec6628e3974b",
          "url": "https://github.com/VowpalWabbit/vowpal_wabbit/commit/e1527704acf841cc8e0678fec088e70e66012416"
