          "message": "test: add 185 unit tests to push line coverage to 90%+ (#4849)\n\n* test: add 185 unit tests to push line coverage from 87.5% to 90.1%\n\nAdd comprehensive coverage tests targeting 40+ reductions and core\ncomponents including LDA, FTRL, marginal, bootstrap, OAA, nn, cbify,\ncs_active, search, epsilon_decay, freegrad, topk, stagewise_poly, and\nmany others. Document a genuine bug in confidence_sequence_robust where\nIPS-estimated rewards can exceed [0,1] bounds via ASSERT_DEATH test.\n\n* fix: clamp out-of-range rewards in epsilon_decay to prevent assertion failure\n\nconfidence_sequence_robust::update() asserts 0 <= r <= 1, but\nepsilon_decay was passing unclamped CB costs as rewards. Now clamps\nto [0,1] with a warning instead of crashing.\n\n* fix: suppress -Wdeprecated-declarations in tests exercising deprecated APIs\n\nTests for cmd_string_replace_value, VW::initialize(string), and\nVW::finish() intentionally call deprecated functions for coverage.\nWrap with pragma to avoid -Werror failures in CI.\n\n* fix: fix ASAN/UBSAN/valgrind failures in coverage tests\n\n- CostSensitiveCoverage3.WithNamedLabels: use named label format\n  (cat:0.5) instead of numeric (1:0.5) to avoid triggering\n  heap-buffer-overflow in csoaa.cc predict path with 0-indexed labels\n- ReductionsCoverage3.FtrlPistolWithAudit: remove --audit flag to\n  avoid uninitialized bool read in gd.cc audit path with --pistol\n\n* fix: fix csoaa off-by-one overflow and uninitialized weights.adaptive\n\n- csoaa.cc: 0-indexed multipredict loop used `i <= num_classes` causing\n  heap-buffer-overflow on pred[num_classes]. Changed to `i < num_classes`.\n- array_parameters.h: initialize `adaptive` and `normalized` to false\n  so reductions like FTRL/pistol that don't set them don't cause\n  undefined behavior when audit reads them.\n- Restore original test forms that exercise these code paths.\n\n* ci: add cmake configure retry to vcpkg_build workflow\n\nReplace single lukka/run-cmake step with separate configure/build/test\nsteps. Configure retries up to 3 times with 30s delays to handle\ntransient vcpkg download failures (SSL errors, network timeouts).\nMatches the retry pattern already used in asan.yml.",
          "timestamp": "2026-02-01T14:38:22-05:00",
