          "id": "93ffd854fc9d37265c39cf7b264bbfade1ce3c10",
          "message": "test: add 42 unit tests for coverage batch 8 (+118 lines) (#4854)\n\n* test: add 42 unit tests for coverage batch 8 (+118 lines)\n\nTarget code paths unreachable from CLI/E2E tests, verified with\nlcov after running both unit tests and all 725 E2E tests.\n\nCovered areas:\n- global_data.cc: dump_weights_to_json_experimental() all paths\n- marginal.cc: --compete mode save/load of expert_state\n- io_buf.cc: isbinary(), copy_to(), replace_buffer(), readto\n- vw_validate.cc: all validation error paths\n- autolink.cc: predict-only path\n- array_parameters_{dense,sparse}.cc: set_zero, shallow_copy, share\n- merge.cc: merge_deltas warning/error paths\n- api_status.cc: try_clear\n- best_constant.cc: quantile loss paths\n- named_labels.cc: copy assignment operator\n- unique_sort.cc: unique_sort_features\n- crossplat_compat.cc: get_pid\n- label_dictionary.cc: append/truncate_from_memory\n- version.cc: from_string\n- cost_sensitive.cc: CSOAA output paths\n\nBaseline: 90.0% (26271/29190), New: 90.4% (26389/29190)\n\n* fix: remove redundant nested sparse check in validate_num_bits\n\nThe inner `if (all.weights.sparse)` on line 41 was always true\nsince it was already inside an identical outer check on line 39.",
