          "distinct": true,
          "id": "f7414e21759b6781abfbba4c004ebb9b8232e197",
          "message": "feat(cs): downgrade from .NET Standard 2.1 to 2.0 (#4865)\n\n* feat(cs): downgrade from .NET Standard 2.1 to 2.0\n\nThis enables compatibility with .NET Framework 4.6.1+, which was not\npossible with .NET Standard 2.1.\n\nChanges:\n- Update all .csproj files to target netstandard2.0\n- Replace Stream.Read/Write(Span<byte>) calls with byte[] overloads\n  since the Span-based overloads don't exist in .NET Standard 2.0\n\nThe System.Memory package (already referenced) provides Span<T> support\nfor .NET Standard 2.0.\n\n* feat(cs): multi-target netstandard2.0 and 2.1 for efficiency\n\nUse #if NETSTANDARD2_1_OR_GREATER to select efficient Span-based\nStream.Read/Write on .NET Standard 2.1+, while falling back to\nbyte[] buffer approach on .NET Standard 2.0.\n\nThis gives best of both worlds:\n- .NET Framework 4.6.1+ compatibility (via netstandard2.0)\n- Efficient zero-copy IO on .NET Core 3.0+ (via netstandard2.1)\n\n* fix(cs): downgrade to netstandard2.0 for .NET Framework compatibility\n\n- Target netstandard2.0 instead of 2.1 for broader compatibility\n- Add #if NETSTANDARD2_1_OR_GREATER for efficient Span code path\n- Use byte[] temp buffer fallback for 2.0 (no Span overloads)\n- Replace ??= with explicit null checks for C# 7.3 compatibility\n- Rename shadowed parameter to avoid CS0136\n\n* docs(cs): add deprecation notice for C++/CLI bindings\n\n- Add #pragma message warning when compiling C++/CLI bindings\n- Add README.md explaining both binding options\n- Point users to the cross-platform .NET Standard bindings",
          "timestamp": "2026-02-05T20:19:16-05:00",
          "tree_id": "574dbb883a1cae8f5bd64384caad2d588631a2c5",
          "url": "https://github.com/VowpalWabbit/vowpal_wabbit/commit/f7414e21759b6781abfbba4c004ebb9b8232e197"
