          "id": "dd762f8664552ce821694dee2b0e72218c59d7bc",
          "message": "test: add 1,277 unit tests to maximize code coverage (#4876)\n\n* ci: add lcov artifact upload to coverage workflow\n\nAdd lcov report generation and artifact upload steps so we can\ndownload per-file coverage data from gcc 13 and identify the\nspecific files that need targeted tests to reach 90%+ coverage.\n\n* fix: add --ignore-errors unused to lcov for newer lcov versions\n\nlcov 2.x on Ubuntu 24.04 treats unused exclude patterns as fatal\nerrors. Add --ignore-errors unused to tolerate patterns that don't\nmatch any captured files.\n\n* Add 1,277 unit tests to maximize code coverage\n\nAdd 10 new test files covering all major VW subsystems:\n- coverage_numeric_reductions_test.cc (158 tests): LDA, KSVM, BFGS, CS Active, GD MF, Stagewise Poly\n- coverage_search_test.cc (112 tests): search core, entity relation, dep parser, graph, metatasks\n- coverage_text_parser_test.cc (154 tests): text parser, parser dispatch, parse_args, parse_primitives\n- coverage_label_parser_test.cc (154 tests): cost-sensitive, multiclass, CB, slates, multilabel, simple\n- coverage_cb_explore_test.cc (129 tests): cbify, OAA, explore algorithms, warm CB, synthcover\n- coverage_core_framework_test.cc (116 tests): learner, VW init, GD variants, parse_regressor, workspace\n- coverage_config_io_test.cc (133 tests): option validation, CLI parsing, logger, IO adapters, IO buf\n- coverage_json_parser_test.cc (100 tests): JSON labels, features, DSJson, slates JSON, audit mode\n- coverage_misc_reductions_test.cc (122 tests): CSOAA LDF, ECT, BS, NN, FTRL, Active, LRQ, Freegrad\n- coverage_automl_trees_test.cc (99 tests): memory tree, EMT, PLT, automl, epsilon decay, CCB, CATS tree\n\nAlso removes dead code: quake_inv_sqrt() in gd.cc (zero callers, wrapped in unused-function warning pragmas).\n\nBugs found during testing (documented as TODOs/DISABLED tests):\n- dep_parser cost_to_go doesn't validate action space vs --search size\n- selective_branching metatask + sequencespan triggers learner ft_offset assertion\n- CBZO multi-example triggers clamp assertion (NaN propagation)\n\n* fix: four bugs found by new coverage tests\n\nCBZO: guard against numerical instability when action is close to\ncentroid. The gradient estimate cost/(action-centroid) explodes when the\ndenominator is near zero, producing inf/NaN that corrupts weights and\nmin_label/max_label. Clamp |denom| to at least radius, bounding the\ngradient to the maximum that the intended exploration distribution\ncould produce. Also reject radius < 1e-3 at setup with a warning.\n\ndep_parser: auto-compute minimum num_actions when cost_to_go is enabled.\nThe action space encodes transition+label pairs, requiring at least\n1+2*num_label actions (arc-standard) or 2+2*num_label (arc-eager).\n\nsearch BaseTask::Run(): save/restore ft_offset on examples so metatasks\nthat call Run() multiple times (selective_branching) don't accumulate\noffset drift that triggers underflow assertions in learner.cc.\n\nsequence_ctg: guard against out-of-bounds access in costs vector when\noracle label is 0 (unlabeled/end-of-sequence) or exceeds num_actions.\ncosts[oracle-1]=0 segfaults when oracle is 0 due to unsigned underflow.\n\nEnables 3 previously disabled CBZO tests and restores 2 search tests.\n\n* fix(cbzo): use tight MIN_DENOM threshold instead of radius for gradient clamp\n\nThe previous clamp (|denom| < radius) triggered on normal training data\nwhen the centroid approached logged actions, changing numeric outputs and\ncausing cross-platform test failures. Use 1e-6 absolute threshold instead\nto only guard against truly dangerous near-zero denominators.\n\n* fix(gd): restore quake_inv_sqrt needed by WASM and non-SIMD builds\n\nThe function was incorrectly removed as dead code. It is used as a\nfallback when neither SSE2 nor NEON is available (e.g., WASM/Emscripten\nand ARM cibuildwheel builds).\n\n* fix: cb_explore_adf_cover heap-buffer-overflow and KSVM memory leak\n\nTwo bugs fixed:\n\n1. Test helpers incorrectly included the newline example in multi_ex\n   passed to learn/predict. With DR cost estimation, gen_cs_example_dr\n   skips newlines producing fewer costs than preds.size(), causing\n   out-of-bounds access in cb_explore_adf_cover's loop. Fixed by\n   separating newline from multi_ex (matching established VW pattern).\n\n2. workspace::~workspace() never called l->finish(), so reduction\n   finish callbacks (e.g. finish_kernel_svm which frees pool entries)\n   never ran when workspace was destroyed via unique_ptr. Fixed by\n   adding l->finish() to the destructor and making learner::finish()\n   idempotent.\n\n* ci: split valgrind unit tests into 3 parallel jobs\n\nWith ~2,177 unit tests, a single valgrind job was taking ~3x longer\nthan other CI jobs. Split into 3 segments using ctest -I stride to\ninterleave tests evenly across parallel jobs.",
