          "id": "ca578a28baed76e4e9a464f258009d2ea84132c5",
          "message": "ci: add ccache to ASAN/UBSAN builds (#4877)\n\nThe macos-15-intel ASAN job is the slowest CI at ~31 minutes,\nrebuilding all C++ from scratch each run. Add ccache with GitHub\nActions cache to reuse object files across runs.\n\nChanges:\n- Install ccache on Linux (apt) and macOS (brew)\n- Cache ccache directory via actions/cache with per-OS/preset keys\n- Pass CMAKE_C/CXX_COMPILER_LAUNCHER=ccache to cmake configure\n- Show ccache stats after build for monitoring hit rates\n\nFirst run will be all cache misses (same speed). Subsequent runs\non the same OS/preset should see significant speedups from cache\nhits, similar to the ~43% improvement seen in cibuildwheel macOS.",
