          "distinct": true,
          "id": "33f342e5e58993f0204bc602da1dcefea06a3e97",
          "message": "ci: switch Windows cibuildwheel to Ninja + ccache (#4878)\n\n* ci: switch Windows cibuildwheel to Ninja + ccache\n\nReplace the Visual Studio 2019 generator with Ninja for the Windows\nwheel build. This enables ccache for compiler output caching across\nthe 5 Python version builds (cp310-cp314), significantly reducing\ntotal build time since the C++ code is identical across versions.\n\nChanges:\n- Add ilammy/msvc-dev-cmd to set up MSVC environment for Ninja\n- Install ccache via Chocolatey\n- Switch CMAKE_GENERATOR from \"Visual Studio 16 2019\" to \"Ninja\"\n- Add CMAKE_C/CXX_COMPILER_LAUNCHER=ccache flags\n- Set CCACHE_BASEDIR via github.workspace for path normalization\n\n* fix: use sccache instead of ccache on Windows\n\nccache fails on Windows with \"Filename too long\" due to the 260-char\nMAX_PATH limit when handling MSVC compiler paths. Switch to sccache\n(Mozilla's compiler cache) which handles MSVC/Windows paths correctly.\n\n* fix: handle Ninja output path and sccache dir on Windows\n\nTwo fixes:\n- setup.py: Add fallback for single-config generators (Ninja) which\n  output to python/ instead of python/Release/ (multi-config VS)\n- pyproject.toml: Use forward slash for SCCACHE_DIR to avoid\n  backslash being stripped by cibuildwheel environment handling\n\n* ci: rebalance valgrind unit tests (4 jobs) and split big-tests (2 jobs)\n\nValgrind unit tests: 3 → 4 parallel jobs to reduce wall clock from\n~28m to ~22m (7m build + ~15m tests).\n\nBig-tests: split into 2 parallel jobs to reduce wall clock from ~27m\nto ~17m. Segment 1 runs MNIST/Covertype/URLRep, segment 2 runs\nMovieLens/OCR. Each segment only downloads the datasets it needs.\n\nGoal: make cibuildwheel.macos-15-intel (~24m) the CI latency leader.",
          "timestamp": "2026-02-09T15:21:05Z",
          "tree_id": "ee435aef1f2a8d8efb12dc263e1683740da59496",
