          "distinct": true,
          "id": "b72fe1a8371e9267c7f9b6ceed820236b80104c9",
          "message": "chore: update dependencies and remove deprecated API usage (#4879)\n\n* chore: update dependencies and remove deprecated API usage\n\n- Update boost_math 1.79.0 → 1.90.0, armadillo 12.1.90 → 14.4.4\n- Migrate vw.cc off deprecated API (13 → 2 suppression sites)\n- Modernize memory_tree.cc serialization to use model_utils API\n- Remove stale TODO comments from vw.h\n\n* chore: remove stale TODOs and unused includes\n\n- Remove dense_parameters::first() (duplicate of data()), migrate all\n  callers in accumulate.cc, multi_model_utils.h, automl_weights_test.cc\n- Remove stale TODO comments: temporary fix notes that are actually\n  correct code (example.cc, search_multiclasstask.cc), outdated\n  personal references (cb_adf.cc), misleading notes where the code\n  already does the right thing (ccb_label.cc, oaa.cc)\n- Remove dead commented-out assertions in automl_test.cc\n- Remove unused #include cb_adf.h and gd.h from epsilon_decay.cc\n  and automl.cc\n\n* chore: remove more stale and answered TODO comments\n\n- Remove answered logger TODOs in plt.cc, search_meta.cc,\n  search_sequencetask.cc, print.cc (all already use trace_message)\n- Remove stale TODOs: kernel_svm.cc init check (handled by early\n  return), gen_cs_example.cc clipping note (safety measure, not a bug),\n  lrq.cc memory leak concern (proper move semantics), ect.cc option\n  validation (already uses .one_of()), ect.cc error level question\n  (error is correct for internal invariant violation)\n- Rewrite count_label.cc TODO as explanatory comment\n- Rewrite nn.cc confused comment as descriptive note\n\n* chore: address substantial TODO items across reductions\n\n- Deduplicate binary_search(): extract identical implementations from\n  cs_active.cc, cb_explore_adf_regcb.cc, and cb_explore_adf_squarecb.cc\n  into shared header confidence_sequence_utility.h\n- scorer.cc: thread step parameter through multipredict instead of\n  hardcoding 0, fixing weight vector offset for multi-model predictions\n- nn.cc: guard hidden bias constant feature setup with add_constant\n  check so --noconstant flag is respected\n- parser.cc: replace deprecated POSIX daemon() with fork()+setsid()\n- memory_tree.cc: replace all std::cout with trace_message guarded by\n  --quiet, fixing output suppression\n\n* style: fix clang-format issues\n\n- Indent preprocessor directives inside blocks with #  prefix\n- Sort includes alphabetically (setup_base.h)\n- Fix operator<< line break alignment for trace_message\n- Collapse short if-body to single line\n\n* style: fix remaining clang-format alignment in memory_tree.cc\n\n* fix: revert scorer multipredict step parameter change\n\nThe second parameter to learner::multipredict() is 'lo' (starting\noffset), not 'step' (stride). The base learner handles stride\ninternally, so passing step as lo broke all multi-class predictions\n(oaa, ect, etc.) by starting from the wrong weight offset.\n\n* test: update memory_tree reference files for cout→trace_message\n\nOutput moved from stdout to stderr, and typos fixed:\n- \"initiazliation\" → \"initialization\"\n- \"strored\" → \"stored\"",
          "timestamp": "2026-02-09T21:25:10-05:00",
          "tree_id": "97b70f278324dd08d76818f896c7e25d97a118be",
