          "distinct": true,
          "id": "cb5df7a2a9fb64a2cb13b6ba63795f7f74688349",
          "message": "chore: fix bugs, remove stale TODOs, and improve logging infrastructure (#4883)\n\n* chore: fix bugs, remove stale TODOs, and improve logging infrastructure\n\nBug fixes:\n- Fix csoaa_ldf holdout loss routing: use per-example test_only instead\n  of global holdout_set_off flag (matches OAA pattern)\n- Fix automl_oracle insert_config fall-through after std::move: add\n  missing queue push and early return to prevent use-after-move\n- Add runtime warning in LRQ setup when a namespace appears in multiple\n  pairs (potential weight collision)\n\nStale TODO removal across 11 files:\n- nn.cc: remove 3 stale TODOs (audit implemented, reserved namespace,\n  move semantics fix)\n- csoaa_ldf.cc: remove 3 stale TODOs (passthrough, partial_prediction,\n  singleline removed)\n- log_multi.cc, memory_tree.cc: remove stale logging tech debt notes\n- automl_impl.cc: remove 2 stale design questions\n- conditional_contextual_bandit.cc: remove 2 stale questions\n- search.cc: remove 4 stale items (beam removed, NOPRED exists, etc.)\n- Update lda_core.cc FIXME and kernel_svm.cc TODO to clarifying NOTEs\n\nFeature implementations:\n- Add --cs_absolute_loss option for CSOAA/CSOAA_LDF to report absolute\n  cost as loss instead of relative (cost - min_cost)\n- Convert bfgs.cc fprintf calls to VW logger (trace_message for stderr\n  progress, logger.out_info for stdout convergence messages)\n- Convert search.cc print_update_search fprintf to trace_message with\n  fmt::format\n- Convert stagewise_poly.cc #ifdef DEBUG blocks to VW debug logging\n  infrastructure (VW_DEBUG_LOG constexpr flag)\n\n* fix: update reference files, fix C++14 compat, and apply clang-format\n\n- Update BFGS stdout reference files for [info] prefix from logger.out_info()\n- Fix leading newline in BFGS termination message (separate blank line)\n- Remove trailing newline from CURV_MESSAGE (spdlog adds its own)\n- Update help reference files for new --cs_absolute_loss option\n- Add LRQ namespace collision warning to 0080.stdout reference\n- Replace C++17 structured bindings with C++14-compatible code in lrq.cc\n- Mark unused 'all' parameter in csoaa_ldf.cc\n- Apply clang-format-14 to all modified source files\n\n* fix: wrap sort_data_compar in #ifdef DEBUG to avoid unused function warning\n\nClang with -Werror,-Wunneeded-internal-declaration flags sort_data_compar\nas unused when VW_DEBUG_LOG is false (constexpr dead code elimination).\nWrapping both the function and its call site in #ifdef DEBUG is consistent\nwith the approach used for debug struct members in the same file.",
          "timestamp": "2026-02-18T09:54:49-05:00",
          "tree_id": "f36ccfb089ffca1bf380df3d2c23c5ecb15bcfb6",
          "url": "https://github.com/VowpalWabbit/vowpal_wabbit/commit/cb5df7a2a9fb64a2cb13b6ba63795f7f74688349"
