          "id": "3642774d21dda7a809714d5ee10a13aa6fece948",
          "message": "ci: add zizmor workflow to audit GitHub Actions for security issues (#4918)\n\nzizmor is a static analyzer for GitHub Actions workflow files. It catches\ntemplate injection (the bug we just fixed in python_checks.yml), pull_request_target\nmisuse, unpinned third-party actions, excessive token permissions, and similar\nclasses of CI security issue at PR review time.\n\nFindings upload as SARIF and surface in the GitHub Security tab alongside\nexisting CodeQL alerts.\n\nTriggers: pushes to master, all PRs, weekly schedule, and manual dispatch.\nBoth actions pinned by commit SHA per zizmor's own guidance.",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-04T21:45:42-04:00",
          "tree_id": "2a481c94832f41b1b4c6d4e3ac32cb2556e31eee",
