          "distinct": true,
          "id": "59f3f6e1e84225ebdbb5ab1ddce583003374e7f9",
          "message": "fix(ci): repair CI after auditwheel and CMake 4.4 drift (#4933)\n\n* fix(ci): repair CI after auditwheel and CMake 4.4 drift\n\nTwo more toolchain rolls have broken master since #4927. Neither is\ncaused by anything in the repo, and both hit every open PR.\n\n1. Build python wheel (current) and (master)\n\n    ValueError: patchelf 0.14.3 found.\n    auditwheel repair requires patchelf >= 0.14.5.\n\nBoth jobs run on ubuntu-22.04, whose patchelf is 0.14.3, and both install\nauditwheel unpinned, so they now pick up a version that has raised its\npatchelf floor above what the image provides. Install patchelf from pip\nalongside auditwheel (currently 0.19.1) so the version is decoupled from\nthe runner image.\n\nThat the \"(master)\" job fails is what identifies this as drift rather\nthan a regression: it builds master's code, freshly cloned, and fails\njust the same.\n\n2. benchmark\n\n    CMake Error: The warning category \"old-style-cast\" is not known.\n\nrun_benchmarks uses lukka/get-cmake@latest, which now installs CMake\n4.4.2. The benchmark port in our ext_libs/vcpkg pin (2026-01-14, port\nversion 1.9.4) passes -Werror=old-style-cast as a cmake option rather\nthan as a compiler flag. Older CMake ignored it; CMake >= 4.4 validates\nthe warning category and errors out. Upstream vcpkg dropped that option\nin benchmark 1.9.5.\n\nPin that one job to CMake 3.31.x rather than bumping ext_libs/vcpkg. The\npin is seven months old and also carries fmt 12.1.0; moving it forward\npulls in fmt 12.2.0, which breaks both VW's own sources (fixed by #4922)\nand the vendored spdlog (fixed by #4931). Refreshing vcpkg is worth doing\nbut it is a coupled change that belongs behind those two, not in a CI\nrepair. The pin is commented so it can be dropped then.\n\n* fix(ci): bound every job's runtime and make apt non-interactive\n\nJobs have been hanging on `sudo apt-get` steps for 60-100 minutes at a\ntime: Linux only, intermittent, spread across every workflow that installs\npackages, while GitHub reported Actions fully operational.\n\nThe cause is not established. The first version of this commit assumed a\ndebconf/needrestart prompt with no tty to answer it, and set\nDEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive and NEEDRESTART_MODE=a to dismiss it. Two\njobs then hung in exactly the same way on the very commit that set those,\nso that explanation is wrong. What remains is apt blocking on something\noutside the runner's control, most plausibly a package mirror, which no\nfrontend setting affects.\n\nSince the hang cannot be prevented from here, bound it instead. No\nworkflow set timeout-minutes, so a stuck job held a runner for GitHub's\ndefault of six hours before failing. Every job now carries a 90 minute\ncap. That is generous against the slowest job observed (benchmark, ~26m)\nand against a cold-cache vcpkg build, while turning a six hour burn into a\nprompt failure that can be re-run.\n\nThe two apt environment variables are kept as ordinary hygiene for\nunattended installs. They are not a fix for this hang and are not claimed\nto be.",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-17T20:57:06-04:00",
          "tree_id": "d76da4e8588c9bab2aac03c88de86184a29ca334",
