          "id": "f859e5f9fdf2adb658a416f4c671bac98221f31a",
          "message": "build: bump vendored spdlog to v1.17.0 for fmt 12.2.0 compatibility (#4931)\n\nWhen VW is built against an external fmt it defines SPDLOG_FMT_EXTERNAL\n(ext_libs/ext_libs.cmake), and on that path spdlog v1.15.0 includes\n<fmt/core.h>. fmt 12.2.0 changed what that header pulls in:\n\n    // fmt <= 12.1.0       // fmt 12.2.0\n    #include \"format.h\"    #include \"base.h\"\n                           #ifdef FMT_DEPRECATED_HEAVY_CORE\n                           #  include \"format.h\"\n                           #endif\n\nfmt::basic_format_string also moved to <fmt/xchar.h>. Neither is reachable\nthrough <fmt/core.h> any more, so spdlog/common.h fails to compile:\n\n    spdlog/common.h:369:54: error: 'basic_format_string' is not a member of 'fmt'\n    spdlog/common.h:369:54: error: 'spdlog::details::to_string_view' redeclared\n      as different kind of entity\n\nv1.17.0 drops the <fmt/core.h> include and relies on <fmt/format.h> alone,\nfixing this upstream.\n\nThis does not affect CI, which passes FMT_SYS_DEP=Off in every workflow\n(vendored fmt 11.0.2) and pins vcpkg's fmt at 12.1.0. It matters to\ndownstream packagers building against a system fmt >= 12.2.0, which\ndistributions and Homebrew already ship.\n\nIt is necessary but not sufficient on its own: VW's own sources include\n<fmt/core.h> the same way, which #4922 fixes separately.\n\nVerified locally with CMake 4.4.2:\n  - vendored fmt 11.0.2 at C++14 (VW's default): builds clean, 2431/2431\n    unit tests pass\n  - system fmt 12.2.0: spdlog compiles cleanly where v1.15.0 produced 28\n    errors; the only failures left are VW's own, and with #4922 applied on\n    top the full build succeeds with zero errors",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-17T23:33:01-04:00",
          "tree_id": "522716ff0c323d9e5d9c3f7eda27bac33afaeeb4",
          "url": "https://github.com/VowpalWabbit/vowpal_wabbit/commit/f859e5f9fdf2adb658a416f4c671bac98221f31a"
