          "id": "2f28fb1e00a53b6bfcdbab297eb701ea8eb426ad",
          "message": "build: bump googletest to v1.16.0 for CMake 4.x forward compatibility (#4930)\n\ngoogletest v1.13.0 declares `cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.5)`, which\nmakes CMake 4.x emit, once per googletest CMakeLists.txt:\n\n  CMake Deprecation Warning at _deps/googletest-src/CMakeLists.txt:4\n  (cmake_minimum_required):\n    Compatibility with CMake < 3.10 will be removed from a future version\n    of CMake.\n\nIt is the only dependency in the tree still below that line. VW itself\ndeclares 3.10 (CMakeLists.txt) and 3.11 (cmake/VowpalWabbitUtils.cmake),\nand every ext_libs submodule already declares 3.8 or newer. When CMake\ndrops <3.10 compatibility this becomes a hard configure error, and the\nexisting -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5 override in the workflows\ndoes not help -- 3.5 would itself be below the new floor and have to be\nraised to 3.10.\n\nv1.16.0 declares `cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.13)` in all three of\nits CMakeLists.txt files, so the warnings disappear entirely.\n\nv1.16.0 is deliberately not the newest release. It is the last one that\nrequires only C++14: v1.17.0 sets `target_compile_features(PUBLIC\ncxx_std_17)`, which would break VW's default build, since VW_CXX_STANDARD\ndefaults to 14 and the macOS standalone job builds and runs the unit tests\nat that default.\n\nVerified locally with CMake 4.4.2 at C++14 (the default) and at C++17:\nconfigure emits zero deprecation warnings, down from three, and all 2431\nunit tests pass in both configurations.",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-18T06:59:14-04:00",
          "tree_id": "69f617964b89e32dff6184f14c329b08f5a0b981",
          "url": "https://github.com/VowpalWabbit/vowpal_wabbit/commit/2f28fb1e00a53b6bfcdbab297eb701ea8eb426ad"
