          "distinct": true,
          "id": "ec8e31c1ecae99e3ce47568644b78b53e07eae01",
          "message": "fix(ci): let the benchmark job report perf alerts instead of 403ing (#4938)\n\nrun_benchmarks sets comment-on-alert, which posts a PR review, but the job\ngrants only contents: write and deployments: write. So whenever a benchmark\ncrosses the alert threshold the action fails with\n\n    POST /repos/VowpalWabbit/vowpal_wabbit/pulls/4930/reviews\n    403 Resource not accessible by integration\n\ninstead of reporting what regressed. The job was already going to fail via\nfail-on-alert; the missing permission just replaced a useful alert with an\nopaque API error. Seen on #4930.\n\nGrant pull-requests: write so the alert can actually be posted.\n\nThat is not sufficient on its own: a fork PR's GITHUB_TOKEN is read-only\nwhatever the permissions block says, so commenting there can only ever 403.\nGate comment-on-alert on the PR coming from this repo. fail-on-alert is\nuntouched, so a fork PR that regresses still fails the job -- it just does\nnot try to write a comment it has no permission to write.",
