          "distinct": true,
          "id": "a3e2f1efe2af7e1f3666a562825a312be4e2eb54",
          "message": "ci: least-privilege token permissions and no credential persistence (#4940)\n\nRebased onto master after #4932 landed. This is the content of #4935, which\nwas merged into the jcl/vw-zizmor-hardening branch rather than into master,\nso it never reached the default branch.\n\nexcessive-permissions (55 findings)\n-----------------------------------\nTwenty of the twenty-one workflows declared no `permissions:` block, so every\njob ran with whatever the repository default grants -- historically\nread-write across contents, issues, pull requests, packages and more. A\ncompromised action or a command injection in any build step inherited that.\n\nEach of those workflows now declares `permissions: contents: read` at the top\nlevel, placed after the `env:` blocks #4933 added so the file reads\non / concurrency / env / permissions / jobs. The jobs that genuinely need\nmore keep their existing job-level grants, which override the default:\n\n  codeql-analysis.analyze       security-events: write   (uploads SARIF)\n  zizmor.zizmor                 security-events: write   (uploads SARIF)\n  run_benchmarks.benchmark      contents: write,         (pushes gh-pages,\n                                pull-requests: write      comments alerts)\n  dotnet_nugets.benchmark_nuget contents: write          (pushes gh-pages)\n\nThe pull-requests: write that #4938 added to run_benchmarks is preserved.\n\ncheck_pr_title.check gets a new job-level grant. It reads the pull request\nand, with validateSingleCommit, its commit list, so it needs\npull-requests: read; it checks nothing out, so it does not need contents.\n\nConfirmed nothing else reaches the API with GITHUB_TOKEN: the two gh-pages\npushes use an explicit tokenized remote URL, every actions/github-script step\nonly calls core.exportVariable, and the docs deploy and coverage upload\nauthenticate with their own secrets (DOCS_DEPLOY_TOKEN, CODECOV_TOKEN).\n\nartipacked (48 findings)\n------------------------\nactions/checkout leaves the token in .git/config as an http.extraheader by\ndefault. It stays there for the rest of the job, so any later step -- or an\nartifact that sweeps up .git -- can read it. All 48 checkouts that did not\nsay otherwise now set persist-credentials: false.\n\nNothing depended on the persisted credential. The submodules are public (the\none relative URL, ext_libs/vcpkg, resolves to microsoft/vcpkg), the\n`git fetch --unshallow --tags` calls read a public repository, and the two\npushes carry their token in the remote URL. The checkouts that do need it --\nthe VowpalWabbit/docs deploy in python_checks, and the sparse checkouts\n#4936 added -- already declared their own setting and are untouched.\n\nVerified structurally afterwards: all 52 checkout steps declare\npersist-credentials, exactly one is true, and no non-checkout step picked the\nkey up by accident.\n\nzizmor findings on master: 103 -> 0 under the 1.24.1 the audit action runs\ntoday, and 103 -> 1 under 1.29.0, the remaining note being adhoc-packages.",
