          "id": "5b2bc762c2ab7841fd260c55f80ad1436a2432a1",
          "message": "build: refresh vcpkg to 2026.07.29 and drop the CMake pin (#4939)\n\nThe vcpkg pin was from 2026-01-14. Refreshing it was blocked until now\nbecause it carries fmt 12.2.0, which needs both #4922 (VW's own sources\nstopped getting fmt::format through <fmt/core.h>) and #4931 (the vendored\nspdlog had the same problem). Both are merged, so this is unblocked.\n\nMove ext_libs/vcpkg to the 2026.07.29 release tag and update\nbuiltin-baseline to the same commit. The versions that change for us:\n\n    fmt          12.1.0     -> 12.2.0\n    benchmark    1.9.4      -> 1.9.5\n    zlib         1.3.1      -> 1.3.2\n    boost-math   1.90.0     -> 1.91.0\n    flatbuffers  25.9.23    -> 25.12.19\n    spdlog, eigen3, rapidjson, gtest unchanged\n\nbenchmark 1.9.5 drops the bogus -Werror=old-style-cast cmake option, which\nis what #4933 pinned run_benchmarks to CMake 3.31.x to avoid: CMake >= 4.4\nvalidates the warning category and errors out. With the port fixed the pin\nhas no purpose, so remove it and let get-cmake install current CMake again.\n\ngtest is unaffected by the refresh either way: the vcpkg presets set\nVW_GTEST_SYS_DEP=OFF, so tests use the FetchContent copy, not vcpkg's.\n\nVerified locally with CMake 4.4.2, the version whose strictness caused the\noriginal failure, configuring `--preset vcpkg-release -DBUILD_BENCHMARKS=On`\n-- the exact combination that used to fail:\n\n  - configure succeeds with no \"old-style-cast\" error\n  - vcpkg installs fmt 12.2.0 and benchmark 1.9.5\n  - full build clean, 2459/2459 unit tests pass\n  - vw-benchmarks.out builds and runs",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-18T08:55:34-04:00",
          "tree_id": "c8c733cb2dd237dff42fc8f250726d1d00af3501",
          "url": "https://github.com/VowpalWabbit/vowpal_wabbit/commit/5b2bc762c2ab7841fd260c55f80ad1436a2432a1"
